# Check out LF everywhere, including on Windows (where Git defaults to core.autocrlf=true).
# The kernel bundle is generated data: build.rs embeds it with include_str!, the generators slice
# it with newline-sensitive markers, and its text is hashed and compared against recorded output,
# so CRLF in a Windows checkout silently changes what the kernels compile from.
* text=auto eol=lf
